  "id": "COMPOUND:19464 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "Dorsmanin D appears to exert its biological effects on prostate cells through a mechanism involving the targeting of specific enzymes and molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Dorsmanin D acts as a target for two distinct enzymes: SDR family member 9 and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. Both of these enzymes are involved in the metabolism of a complex compound, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which is a known metabolite of steroid hormones. This compound is implicated in prostate cell function and may contribute to pathological processes in prostate cancer. The observed interaction between Dorsmanin D and prostate cells implies that the drug may modulate the activity of these enzymes, potentially altering the metabolic pathways that regulate prostate cell proliferation and survival. The consistent involvement of this compound in the targeting of prostate cells, across multiple pathways, supports a mechanistic link between Dorsmanin D and prostate cell biology.",
